<title>NORWAY: FORECAST-Storebrand 1996 profits seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Storebrand 1996 profits seen down.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Storebrand ASA, Norway's biggest insurer, is expected to post 1996 group profits of 1.16 billion crowns, according to eight analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding figure for 1995 was 1.45 billion.</p>
<p>Two said buy, two said hold while four said sell the share.</p>
<p>On a 12-month period, they saw the share priced at 41.13 crowns compared to 45.10 crowns on Friday.</p>
<p>Storebrand will present the 1996 results on Wednesday.</p>
<p>				     (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>					 average     high     low    1995</p>
<p> Life, Storebrand share	    610	 680	500     582</p>
<p> Non-life insurance		  970     1.115	860   1.184</p>
<p> Other activity		     -428	-334     -470    -267</p>
<p> Group result			1.155     1.282    1.050   1.451</p>
<p> EPS 96 (crowns)		    3.84	4.30     3.40    4.94</p>
<p> EPS 97				 3.92	4.57     2.60</p>
<p> EPS 98				 3.89	4.80     2.80</p>
<p>((--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41))</p>
